<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  The App Group the share extension and the app hand captures through.

	  Separate from Vihara.entitlements on purpose. A target has exactly one
	  entitlements file, and Vihara.entitlements carries Sign in with Apple, which
	  is deliberately NOT wired because referencing it fails every device build
	  until the capability is enabled on the App ID. Merging the two here would
	  break device builds for two reasons instead of one.

	  This one has the same provisioning dependency, and it is worth knowing
	  before the first bug report:

	      the simulator works immediately;
	      a device build needs `group.com.vihara.app` registered on BOTH App IDs
	      (com.vihara.app and com.vihara.app.share) and enabled for both targets.

	  Without it, containerURL(forSecurityApplicationGroupIdentifier:) returns nil
	  and every capture is lost. SharedInbox.isAvailable exists so the extension
	  says so rather than appearing to succeed — see ShareViewController.

	  When Sign in with Apple is finally switched on (Xcode → Signing &
	  Capabilities → + Capability), Xcode writes into whichever file
	  CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS already names — this one. At that point the two files
	  should be merged and Vihara.entitlements deleted.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.vihara.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
